- Oh, yeah.

00:11:03.079 --> 00:11:05.373
- Yeah. And I—Drake was
 supposed to pay you for it.

00:11:05.373 --> 00:11:06.874
But last I heard, he had never paid.

00:11:06.874 --> 00:11:10.586
Did he end up paying?
- Nah, nah, nah, nah.
I ain’t get, I ain’t get straight.

00:11:10.586 --> 00:11:12.588
I think we—no, he did
give me $10,000.

00:11:12.588 --> 00:11:14.840
- OK.
- He did give me $10,000 on that. Yes, he did.

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:16.592
He paid me.
- Yeah. You did an interview with Angie,

00:11:16.592 --> 00:11:17.927
and I remember he was late.

00:11:17.927 --> 00:11:20.763
He hadn't paid up at that point.
- He was late. I was on him for a minute, too.

00:11:20.763 --> 00:11:22.473
I was on him about my lil’ 10

00:11:22.473 --> 00:11:25.726
- All right, so I wanna talk about
your music. Obviously “Culture III,”

00:11:25.726 --> 00:11:28.521
huge hit. We were waiting a minute
for it to come out.

00:11:29.230 --> 00:11:32.108
How do you know when
it's time to drop an album?

00:11:32.775 --> 00:11:35.361
- It was way over time for “Culture III.”

00:11:35.361 --> 00:11:38.030
It was just, like, the pandemic.

00:11:38.030 --> 00:11:40.282
We was tryna figure out
what we wanted to do. And

00:11:42.326 --> 00:11:45.037
I think we had the album right before it dropped.

00:11:45.037 --> 00:11:48.082
We was gonna come the anniversary in 2020.

00:11:48.082 --> 00:11:49.125
But then the pandemic hit.

00:11:49.125 --> 00:11:51.377
That's what kinda, like,
threw everything off.

00:11:51.377 --> 00:11:53.587
Then we had to, like, change the records
because, you know what I’m sayin’, like,

00:11:53.587 --> 00:11:55.965
the timing was just,

00:11:55.965 --> 00:11:58.175
was just crazy cuz, like, just speaking

00:11:58.175 --> 00:12:01.804
the lyrics and the lyrics that you
talkin’ about was just so different

00:12:01.804 --> 00:12:04.640
from what was going on in all the,
like, Black Lives Matter.

00:12:04.640 --> 00:12:07.643
Things start coming up,
and it was just like, “All right, we gotta change it.

00:12:07.643 --> 00:12:08.269
We gotta get right.

00:12:08.269 --> 00:12:09.478
We gotta come back.

00:12:09.478 --> 00:12:12.022
We gotta drop the Juice WRLD
record and talk about,

00:12:12.022 --> 00:12:14.942
you know what I’m sayin’, real-life problems
with drugs. We gotta,

00:12:14.942 --> 00:12:17.069
we gotta come back and drop ‘Vaccine.’”

00:12:17.069 --> 00:12:20.197
And we had to, like, change it up
and go “Avalanche.”

00:12:20.197 --> 00:12:22.199
We had to put the old-school feel with the,

00:12:22.199 --> 00:12:25.035
with the new school and come in
and do our, do our shit on that.

00:12:25.035 --> 00:12:27.747
It was just like, “All right, cool,
we gotta switch it up and drop this

00:12:27.747 --> 00:12:31.292
and let the fans know we here to stay.”
And then we had to, like,

00:12:31.292 --> 00:12:35.463
bring it back to, like, Day 1,
Day 1 Migos Northside shit

00:12:35.463 --> 00:12:39.049
You feel what I'm sayin’?
I felt like we had to put all that in one

00:12:39.049 --> 00:12:40.926
and then we had a chip on our shoulder,

00:12:40.926 --> 00:12:42.887
so “Culture III” it was.

00:12:42.887 --> 00:12:44.638
- There's this, like, challenge, I guess,

00:12:44.638 --> 00:12:49.310
of making your album
always feel like it's of the time.

00:12:49.310 --> 00:12:51.187
And that's kind of why you had to wait

00:12:51.187 --> 00:12:53.522
a little bit for “Culture III” to work.

00:12:53.522 --> 00:12:55.649
Is that accurate to say?
- Right. RIght. Right.

00:12:55.649 --> 00:12:59.487
Not so much the time,
but just, like, just things was goin’ on.

00:12:59.487 --> 00:13:01.822
It was just bad, right, for, like, music.

00:13:01.822 --> 00:13:04.867
I feel like music wasn't even connecting,

00:13:04.867 --> 00:13:06.327
you know what I'm sayin’, in the last year.

00:13:06.327 --> 00:13:10.039
So when I—I put, like, a tweet out.
I was like, “When we drop, I feel like

00:13:10.039 --> 00:13:12.958
the world gonna start rotating again.”
Like, the summer gonna start opening again.

00:13:12.958 --> 00:13:14.960
And I feel like that’s what it did.

00:13:14.960 --> 00:13:16.879
- So when it's times like this,

00:13:16.879 --> 00:13:20.758
I'm sure you are inspired,
for lack of a better word, by certain things, right?

00:13:20.758 --> 00:13:22.802
- Mmhmm.
- Things move you to write.

00:13:22.802 --> 00:13:25.888
They inspire
what you're talking about in the music.

00:13:25.888 --> 00:13:29.433
But is it harder or easier to be an artist, right,

00:13:29.433 --> 00:13:32.311
and write songs in this past year-and-a-half?

00:13:32.311 --> 00:13:33.020
- Yeah, it was really tough

00:13:33.020 --> 00:13:35.022
cuz everything is sensitive right now,

00:13:35.022 --> 00:13:38.609
you know what I’m sayin’? So you don't wanna,
you don't wanna almost speak your mind.

00:13:38.609 --> 00:13:42.446
You wanna speak for the people
too, you know what I’m sayin’? So it's just,

00:13:42.446 --> 00:13:45.991
um...which you just gotta
find the right pocket for it.

00:13:45.991 --> 00:13:48.077
- Mmhmm.
- I think we haven't, we haven't did that yet,

00:13:48.077 --> 00:13:50.996
but I think we gonna get our,
gonna get our moment.

00:13:51.497 --> 00:13:53.833
We had a, we had a song called

00:13:53.833 --> 00:13:56.544
“Crushing America,” but we didn't put it out.
- Why not?

00:13:57.294 --> 00:13:58.546
- I don't know. We didn't—

00:13:58.546 --> 00:14:00.756
I don't know. But it's, it’s hard.

00:14:00.756 --> 00:14:02.424
- What's it about?

00:14:02.716 --> 00:14:03.968
- It's crushing America

00:14:03.968 --> 00:14:07.555
- What is—you know, you like,
you like explaining things

00:14:07.555 --> 00:14:09.640
using the word of the thing you're explaining.
- Cuz I feel like

00:14:09.640 --> 00:14:13.310
once we, once we say that, it’s the picture
that you already gotta paint.
- Yeah.

00:14:13.310 --> 00:14:17.523
- You automatically just imagine
something. But it’s about, like, Takeoff came in

00:14:17.523 --> 00:14:20.609
and was goin’ in about
just, like, what's goin’ on in the world.

00:14:20.609 --> 00:14:23.445
And I came in and sung, like, some bars.

00:14:23.445 --> 00:14:25.573
And Set came—it's like, it's hard.
- Yeah?

00:14:25.573 --> 00:14:27.157
When is it—
- I’ll play it for you one day.

00:14:27.157 --> 00:14:29.410
- When will it come out?
- I don’t know.

00:14:29.410 --> 00:14:32.079
- There's certain rappers where you feel
like they coin certain things.

00:14:32.079 --> 00:14:34.874
You know, people equate
T-Pain and Auto-Tune

00:14:34.874 --> 00:14:36.750
Like, they say that is his invention.

00:14:36.750 --> 00:14:41.005
